---
title: (American) Tamago Kake Gohan
servings: 2
cuisine: Japanese
image: https://i.pinimg.com/originals/e9/64/5e/e9645e100538b95e5fd28f07af566345.jpg
---

> In Japan, this dish usually uses a raw egg, but eggs are processed differently in America, so it is best to prepare it in some way. Sunny Side up is best to allow the yolk to still mix with the rice.

Make your @rice{1%cup}(white, usually calrose) with @seasame oil{}(to taste) and set aside.

Heat up @olive oil{} in a #frying pan{} on medium-low heat.

Add @egg{2} and season as desired. Cook sunny side up.

Add egg to the top of each bowl of rice.

Cover in @?furikake{}, @?cilantro{}, and @?sriracha{} as desired.